Package: wavscat
Title: Wavelet Scattering Transforms for Time Series and Audio
Version: 0.0.0.9000
Authors@R: c(
    person("Aidan", "D. Bindoff", email = "aidan.bindoff@utas.edu.au",
           role = c("aut", "cre")),
    person("Kymatio developers", role = "cph",
           comment = "Filter bank and cascade design, BSD-3-Clause"))
Description: Computes the wavelet scattering transform of one-dimensional
    signals: a cascade of Morlet wavelet convolutions, complex modulus and
    low-pass averaging that yields features stable to deformation and locally
    invariant to translation. Supports time scattering of order zero, one and
    two, and joint time-frequency scattering. The filter bank follows the
    construction of Anden and Mallat (2014) <doi:10.1109/TSP.2014.2326991> as
    implemented in the 'Kymatio' Python package. Everything is computed in the
    Fourier domain using base R, so the package has no compiled dependencies.
License: BSD_3_clause + file LICENSE
